{
  "_comment": [
    "The live WCAG 2.2 Level A and AA success criteria. This is the ONE hand-maintained table in",
    "the harness: everything else about coverage is read from axe-core's own rule metadata at",
    "runtime, so it cannot drift from the pinned version. This table cannot be derived that way,",
    "because a rule's conformance tag (wcag2a, wcag22aa) is the lowest level among ALL the criteria",
    "that rule touches -- it does not assign a level to any individual criterion. Levels have to",
    "come from the WCAG document itself.",
    "",
    "Regenerate when WCAG publishes a new version: parse the Recommendation's conformance-level",
    "markers, bounding each criterion's section at the next 'Success Criterion' heading so a",
    "criterion without a marker cannot inherit the next one's. 4.1.1 Parsing is the case that",
    "catches a naive parse: it is 'Obsolete and removed' and carries no level, so it is absent here",
    "and the live A+AA total is 55 rather than 56."
  ],
